# Force LF on both commit and checkout.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true on Windows rewrites the index to CRLF on
# every `git add`, producing phantom modifications and "LF will be replaced
# by CRLF" warnings even though HEAD and the working tree are already LF.
# .gitattributes entries take precedence over core.autocrlf.
#
# `text=auto` (not `text`) so tracked binaries are content-sniffed and never
# have their bytes normalised.
* text=auto eol=lf
